{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Java 8 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++ code to Java 8 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++ code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <iostream>\nusing namespace std;\ntypedef long long llong;\nconst llong MOD = 1000000007LL;\n\nllong computePower(llong base, llong exponent, llong modulus) {\n    llong result = 1;\n    for (llong i = 0; i < exponent; ++i) {\n        result = (result * base) % modulus;\n    }\n    return result;\n}\n\nllong computeModPower(llong base, llong exponent) {\n    return computePower(base, exponent, MOD);\n}\n\nint main() {\n    llong p, k;\n    cin >> p >> k;\n    \n    llong remainder = k % p;\n    if (remainder == 1) {\n        cout << computeModPower(p, p);\n        return 0;\n    }\n    \n    if (remainder == 0) {\n        cout << computeModPower(p, p - 1);\n        return 0;\n    }\n    \n    llong order = 1;\n    while (true) {\n        if ((p - 1) % order != 0) {\n            ++order;\n            continue;\n        }\n        if (computePower(k, order, p) == 1) {\n            break;\n        }\n        ++order;\n    }\n    \n    cout << computeModPower(p, (p - 1) / order);\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport java.util.Scanner;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static final long MOD = 1000000007L;\n\n    public static long computePower(long base, long exponent, long modulus) {\n        long result = 1;\n        for (long i = 0; i < exponent; ++i) {\n            result = (result * base) % modulus;\n        }\n        return result;\n    }\n\n    public static long computeModPower(long base, long exponent) {\n        return computePower(base, exponent, MOD);\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner scanner = new Scanner(System.in);\n        long p = scanner.nextLong();\n        long k = scanner.nextLong();\n        \n        long remainder = k % p;\n        if (remainder == 1) {\n            System.out.println(computeModPower(p, p));\n            return;\n        }\n        \n        if (remainder == 0) {\n            System.out.println(computeModPower(p, p - 1));\n            return;\n        }\n        \n        long order = 1;\n        while (true) {\n            if ((p - 1) % order != 0) {\n                ++order;\n                continue;\n            }\n            if (computePower(k, order, p) == 1) {\n                break;\n            }\n            ++order;\n        }\n        \n        System.out.println(computeModPower(p, (p - 1) / order));\n    }\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.00014065706636756659, -1.1920922133867862e-06, -3.576278118089249e-07, -0.00013064485392533243, -2.9205850296420977e-05, -0.00045503751607611775, -0.0152143444865942, -2.5510462364763953e-05, -3.814624506048858e-05, -1.4305104514278355e-06, -3.814624506048858e-05, -0.0011714984430000186, -2.825220326485578e-05, -0.8829724192619324, -4.291525328881107e-06, -5.876845170860179e-05, -6.9141146923357155e-06, -1.7881377516459906e-06, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, -5.149708886165172e-05, 0.0, 0.0, -5.960462772236497e-07, 0.0, 0.0, -